   "Northwind-negotiator": "compromising",
   "Halcyon-researcher": "collaborating",
   "Halcyon-drafter": "competing",
   "Halcyon-negotiator": "competing"
  },
  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "S1 is strict, requiring 24-hour reporting for all incidents and 24-hour customer notice. S2 sets a permanent 7% failure limit—above the safe 5%—but requires full per-model results to regulators and purchasing customers, not public publication. S3 requires new-unit shut-off in 24 months (weakened) and 6-year retrofit; S4 requires built-in suppression in 36 months; S5 mandates recall above 8/100k with prompt notice, with no serious-injury clause."
 },
